  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Organizing a Circular Migration Project with Suriname in the Domain of Healthcare</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will facilitate the development of a collaborative and sustainable Skills Mobility Partnership (SMP) where Suriname, in return for tailored financial and technical support provided by the Belgian healthcare sector will provide access to a reliable pool of well-educated Dutch speaking health care workers that can work temporary or permanently in Belgium in hospitals and/or elderly homes. The Belgian employers have committed to provide financial support for the capacity building (in Suriname) and training component (in Belgium) of the SMP. For each successfully recruited worker an amount will be made available for the SMP.  This support can for instance be provided in the form of &#x201C;scholarships&#x201D; to attract and encourage new students to enrol in (specialized) nursing programmes in Surinamese schools, as well as in the form of incentives / top ups for a pool of essential specialist nurses to continue working in Suriname. The Belgian employers are also willing to support COVAB to improve its curricula, teaching practices and training system. The allocation of the Belgian financial means will be further fine-tuned in the inception phase of the project and will be designed as to ensure transparency and integrity in the use of funds.</narrative>
  </description>
